secubox-p2p (1.9.0-1~bookworm1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * feat(macro): M2 macro grant + consumer activate + UI SOCKS endpoint + revoke.
    Provider side: self-certifying Subscription auth over auto offers — consumer
    builds a signed Subscription (ed25519, mirrors verbs.py), POSTs it to the
    provider's mesh listener on wg-mesh :8798 (X-Real-IP validated against the
    consumer's wg-mesh IP). Provider verifies signature, runs macroctl grant,
    returns a credential with the SOCKS endpoint.
    Consumer side: POST /services/{id}/activate pulls the credential over the
    mesh and runs ``sudo -n secubox-macroctl <kind> activate --cred <json>``
    (NoNewPrivileges=no for the sudo macroctl path); the resolved SOCKS endpoint
    is stored in the activation overlay.
    Revoke: POST /services/{id}/revoke-access runs macroctl revoke and clears
    the active state from the overlay.
    Registry: merge_services now surfaces overlay[sid]["endpoint"] in the row
    when present; set_active accepts an optional endpoint= kwarg to persist it.
    UI: for automatable + active + endpoint rows, loadServices() displays the
    SOCKS endpoint (e.g. ``SOCKS 10.10.0.1:9050``) and a "Revoke access" button
    calling revokeAccess() → POST /services/{id}/revoke-access.
    Depends: secubox-annuaire (annuaire catalog + subscription verbs).

